    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20051111.0263\n\nBERLIN, Nov. 11 , 2005 (Xinhua)\n\nGerman Stocks end higher\n\n\n\n\nGerman stocks rose Friday in Frankfurt led by Siemens AG and DaimlerChrysler AG.\n\nThe 30-share benchmark DAX Index jumped 1.50 percent to 5090.75 with 29 stocks rising.\n\nSiemens AG rose 0.97 euros to 63.30 euros after the company sold its stake in Mitsubishi Motors Corp.\n\nDaimlerChrysler AG gained 0.69 euros to 42.65 euros after selling part of its holding in Juniper Networks Inc.\n\nThe index of medium-sized firms, MDAX, rose 0.79 percent to 6992.74 points.\n\nThe index of high-tech stocks, TecDAX, was up 0.77 percent to 581.41 points.",
